[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-77680"] :question/problem "Consider the line $x=5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $x=5$ passes through the points $A(5,0)$ and $B(5,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(-5,0)$ and ${B}^{′}(-4,1).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{1-0}{-4-(-5)}(x-(-5)) \\\\ y & =x+5 \\\\ x-y+5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-281140/field-1/83b1f991cb08df40145f9b1ef79e9e291491185d503944169faaa3e64068c44f" :answer/id #uuid "813777da-7c21-5540-9d09-57659feecf69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x-2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281140/field-1/25ab51c1d74656a6e8aeada130ce71eb48b4ee179c91ebae370e934604a1bd3b" :answer/id #uuid "d84c2a45-c2f3-5cf2-b567-295b70a67bba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-5y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281140/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0515d3d5-630a-5eec-b3d6-9d7749d7bcd9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281140/field-1/83b1f991cb08df40145f9b1ef79e9e291491185d503944169faaa3e64068c44f" :answer-field/choices ["q-281140/field-1/83b1f991cb08df40145f9b1ef79e9e291491185d503944169faaa3e64068c44f" "q-281140/field-1/25ab51c1d74656a6e8aeada130ce71eb48b4ee179c91ebae370e934604a1bd3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281140" :question/id #uuid "87e8ce2c-dfcb-53fd-8d39-6e18379846c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-281140" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=2x-3$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=12.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=2x-3$ passes through the points $A(0,-3)$ and $B(1,-1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(0,-6)$ and ${B}^{′}(2,-1).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{-1+6}{2-0}(x-0) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{5}{2}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+6 & =\\frac{5}{2}x \\\\ 2y+12 & =5x \\\\ 5x-2y & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-281140/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281140"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281236/field-1/dc8da8041e2f0fe9c0d73a2768c0466f7d86e6d9ae35e3af4cf64359c2029916" :answer/id #uuid "48876e20-f769-587d-899b-e540c2004f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x-7y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281236/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5705ca9-05be-5a28-b721-a34551083b33" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281236/field-1/dc8da8041e2f0fe9c0d73a2768c0466f7d86e6d9ae35e3af4cf64359c2029916" :answer-field/choices ["q-281236/field-1/dc8da8041e2f0fe9c0d73a2768c0466f7d86e6d9ae35e3af4cf64359c2029916"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281236" :question/id #uuid "6e5a2374-c8a0-52ba-8347-79e5368d0c7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-281236" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x+1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=15.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x+1$ passes through the points $A(0,1)$ and $B(3,2)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 16 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(2,-1)$ and ${B}^{′}(16,7).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+1 & =\\frac{7-(-1)}{16-2}(x-2) \\\\ y+1 & =\\frac{8}{14}(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+1 & =\\frac{4}{7}(x-2) \\\\ 7y+7 & =4x-8 \\\\ 4x-7y & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-281236/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281236"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281580/field-1/abd8119fcd7dceb08550c6a356ee0c20f59b740345109ac5298d70c862748463" :answer/id #uuid "9038b770-629c-59e3-846f-cd94357fe89e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-4y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281580/field-1/e60d21c1edc1a1b0e54e4a576b7a72542c73c6f5897df42d39415a69184dc369" :answer/id #uuid "fbe94949-ee3d-5dc9-ac5e-b63612d0d720" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x-y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281580/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa02b0c-8b31-5c64-9b56-9d19ff5fb2b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281580/field-1/abd8119fcd7dceb08550c6a356ee0c20f59b740345109ac5298d70c862748463" :answer-field/choices ["q-281580/field-1/abd8119fcd7dceb08550c6a356ee0c20f59b740345109ac5298d70c862748463" "q-281580/field-1/e60d21c1edc1a1b0e54e4a576b7a72542c73c6f5897df42d39415a69184dc369"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281580" :question/id #uuid "a2bac187-b724-5e7f-a90f-46647a5ab6f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-281580" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=-1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=-8.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=-1$ passes through the points $P(0,-1)$ and $Q(1,-1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${P}^{′}(0,2)$ and ${Q}^{′}(4,3).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${P}^{′}$ and ${Q}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-2 & =\\frac{3-2}{4-0}(x-0) \\\\ y-2 & =\\frac{1}{4}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-8 & =x \\\\ x-4y & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-281580/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281580"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281581/field-1/1a9b08e3cfe651d7580c57fec49baa7ff2d33ecc347b1030c376d714c70950e2" :answer/id #uuid "812bd6b3-17b1-527d-8b58-b77ec93b1871" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281581/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f103862-4811-51d6-85cd-845062526155" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281581/field-1/1a9b08e3cfe651d7580c57fec49baa7ff2d33ecc347b1030c376d714c70950e2" :answer-field/choices ["q-281581/field-1/1a9b08e3cfe651d7580c57fec49baa7ff2d33ecc347b1030c376d714c70950e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281581" :question/id #uuid "e4819488-a7a0-5944-ad18-73e05d2e8341" :question/math-academy-id "q-281581" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=3$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=21.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=3$ passes through the points $P(0,3)$ and $Q(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${P}^{′}(9,3)$ and ${Q}^{′}(10,1).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${P}^{′}$ and ${Q}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{1-3}{10-9}(x-9) \\\\ y-3 & =-2(x-9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3 & =-2x+18 \\\\ 2x+y & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-281581/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281581"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
